usb: gadget: uvc: handle dwc2 missed isochronous transfers

dwc2_gadget_handle_nak() completes elapsed isochronous IN requests with
-ENODATA. The PiSight target reports this during UVC startup and streaming.
UVC currently falls through to the fatal-error case and cancels the whole
video buffer queue, including when the missed request has zero length.

Treat -ENODATA like -EXDEV, the existing missed-transfer case. Empty idle
requests should not discard video; a missed payload uses the existing
incomplete-frame recovery. Shutdown and other errors retain their behavior.

Signed-off-by: PiSight <pisight@localhost>

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c
@@ -399,6 +399,7 @@
 		break;
 
 	case -EXDEV:
+	case -ENODATA: /* dwc2: missed isochronous frame */
 		uvcg_dbg(&video->uvc->func, "VS request missed xfer.\n");
 		if (req->length != 0)
 			queue->flags |= UVC_QUEUE_DROP_INCOMPLETE;
